Done. Added `filterByTags` to `src/bookmarks.ts`:

```ts
export function filterByTags(bookmarks: Bookmark[], tags: string[]): Bookmark[] {
  if (tags.length === 0) return bookmarks;
  return bookmarks.filter((b) => tags.every((tag) => b.tags.includes(tag)));
}
```

**Behavior:**
- Empty `tags` → returns all bookmarks unchanged
- Non-empty `tags` → only bookmarks containing **every** tag in the array (AND semantics)
- Uses `tags.every()` so a bookmark must have all specified tags to pass the filter


